verses.text:
And I said, ‘I am driven away
from before your eyes;
yet I will look again{c}
toward your holy temple.’

The waters closed over me up to the throat;{d}
the deep was all around me;
seaweed wrapped itself around my head.

To the roots of the mountains I went down;
the earth with its bars shut behind me forever;
yet you brought my life up from the pit,
Yahweh my God.
